Z||000000||mrgone||08-24-2001||11:57 PM||||Was poking around looking up ford probe problems for a friend when I came up on this site. I thought to myself, wow. Alot of new cars have small problems that dealerships wont admit there is a recall. My freind at work (we work for honda) has a new civic that has window seating problems, and they wanted 150$ to fix it, when there infact was a recall on them. Then I thought of you guys. Always craving more resourses. Do a search on all your friends cars. You WILL and MUST save them money. Auto manufacturers must not get paid for problems they admit to, and charge people to have fixed. <P>well id just like to warn you, the longer a car model is activley on the road, the more time people have to find problems.<P> <A HREF="http://www.alldata.com/recalls/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.alldata.com/recalls/index.html</A> <P><BR>and i looked up a celebrity, they say there is a shoulder harness seat belt kit dealer installed. do they now install real seatbelts where there previousley only lap straps?<P>Honda also requested that site not list recalls for their Acura line of cars, unless you register with them. Things are looking more evil every day. Why cant they see we are just people helping people?<P>Sad.<BR>Enjoy.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">    <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B><p>[This message has been edited by mrgone (edited 08-24-2001).]||||reg||4
